WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
Draw a circle, and a straight line
across it through the centre: a diameter.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.380
Pick any point on the circle.

3
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.950
Join it to both ends of the diameter.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.420
Measure the angle at that top corner.

5
00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.760
Ninety degrees.

6
00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.920
Slide the point round the circle.

7
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.640
Near one end, near the top, anywhere.

8
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.670
Still ninety degrees.

9
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.080
Lucky coincidence?

10
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.590
Or is there a reason it
can never be anything else?

11
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.550
In this mission, you'll
name the parts of a circle:

12
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.440
the centre, a radius,
a diameter and a chord.

13
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:36.640
You'll meet the circle theorems, and the
exact reasons examiners want you to write

14
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.890
for each one.

15
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: explain why the top
corner is always ninety degrees.
